IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-part3-required-period`

-- Tests of Part 3 (regulations 12 to 15B). Expected values were worked out by hand from the text
-- before the file was run.

§ `Tests of regulations 12 and 13`

-- (limited, 3 months) (limited, 9 months) (severe, 3 months) (severe, 9 months) are the four facts of one component.
`limited throughout` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`severe throughout` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`neither throughout` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
-- Limited before the prescribed date, severe after.
`limited then severe` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
-- Limited and severe both reported for the look-back window (an inconsistent report): reg 4(3) makes it severe only.
`both reported in the look-back` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
-- Limited for the first 2 months of the look-back only: "at every time" fails, so the input is FALSE.
`limited for part of the look-back only` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
-- Limited in the look-back, not in the look-forward.
`limited in the look-back only` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
-- Limited in the look-forward, not in the look-back.
`limited in the look-forward only` MEANS `the likely determinations across the two windows` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

-- reg 12(1) and 13(1): standard rate needs limited (and not severely limited) at every time in both windows.
#ASSERT `reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited throughout` `with` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `severe throughout` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `neither throughout` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited then severe` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited in the look-back only` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited in the look-forward only` `with` FALSE)
-- Severely limited in the look-back and limited in the look-forward: the look-back is not "limited" (reg 4(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `both reported in the look-back` `with` FALSE)
-- Reg 15A(4)/15B(4) regard limb (a) as met: the look-forward alone then decides.
#ASSERT `reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited in the look-forward only` `with` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited in the look-back only` `with` TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 13(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the mobility component is met` `limited throughout` `with` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 13(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the mobility component is met` `severe throughout` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 13(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the mobility component is met` `limited then severe` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 13(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the mobility component is met` `limited in the look-forward only` `with` TRUE

-- reg 12(2) and 13(2): enhanced rate needs severely limited ability at every time in both windows.
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `severe throughout` `with` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `limited throughout` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `neither throughout` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `limited then severe` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `limited then severe` `with` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` `limited throughout` `with` TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 13(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the mobility component is met` `severe throughout` `with` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 13(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the mobility component is met` `limited throughout` `with` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 13(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the mobility component is met` `limited then severe` `with` TRUE

-- Facts that fit no one level for part of a window: not "at every time", so not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` `limited for part of the look-back only` `with` FALSE)

-- The rate that follows from which condition is met.
#ASSERT `regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met` TRUE `and` FALSE EQUALS `the standard rate of the component`
#ASSERT `regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met` FALSE `and` TRUE EQUALS `the enhanced rate of the component`
#ASSERT `regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met` FALSE `and` FALSE EQUALS `no rate of the component`
#ASSERT `regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met` TRUE `and` TRUE EQUALS `the enhanced rate of the component`

§ `Tests of regulation 14`

-- reg 14(a): the date of the claim or, if later, the earliest date from which ... is likely, over the previous 3 months.
#ASSERT `reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` (YMD 2025 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2025 6 20)) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 20
#ASSERT `reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` (YMD 2025 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2025 6 10)) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
#ASSERT `reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` (YMD 2025 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2025 6 9)) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
#ASSERT `reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` (YMD 2025 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
-- No such date: the claim date (fork F-13).
#ASSERT `reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` (YMD 2025 6 10) NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
-- reg 14(b): each day of the award.
#ASSERT `reg 14(b): the prescribed date on a day of an award` (YMD 2025 8 17) EQUALS YMD 2025 8 17

§ `Tests of regulation 15`

-- (the benefit of the previous award, the day it ended, the day of the new claim, the number of years, same component, Secretary of State's determination)
-- Ended exactly 2 years before the new claim of 10 June 2025: "not more than 2 years before".
#ASSERT `reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2023 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE
-- One day more than 2 years: not covered by reg 15.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2023 6 9) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE)
-- Under reg 26 the number of years is 1 (the input): 1 year before exactly is within, one day more is not.
#ASSERT `reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10) 1 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2024 6 9) (YMD 2025 6 10) 1 TRUE TRUE)
-- Adult disability payment counts as well as personal independence payment.
#ASSERT `reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `adult disability payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE
-- Other benefits do not.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `some other benefit` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE)
-- An award that ended on the day of the new claim is within; one that ends after it is not an award "ended before".
#ASSERT `reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2025 6 11) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE TRUE)
-- Limb (c): a different component. Limb (d): the Secretary of State does not so determine.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE FALSE)

-- reg 15(2): the 3 months look back from the end of the previous award; the 9 months start the day after the new claim.
#ASSERT (`reg 15(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))'s `the date the 3 months look back from` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT (`reg 15(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))'s `the date the 9 months look forward from` EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
-- reg 15(3): the look-forward date is each day of the award.
#ASSERT (`reg 15(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 7 4))'s `the date the 3 months look back from` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT (`reg 15(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 7 4))'s `the date the 9 months look forward from` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 4
#ASSERT `reg 15(4): regulation 15 is subject to regulation 26` EQUALS "(4) This regulation is subject to regulation 26."

§ `Tests of regulation 15A`

-- Child disability payment, ended not more than 2 years before the claim of 10 June 2025, C aged 16 on the claim date.
#ASSERT `reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` `child disability payment` (YMD 2023 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` `child disability payment` (YMD 2023 6 9) (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 10))
-- 16th birthday one day after the claim: aged 15 on the claim date.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 11))
-- 16th birthday the day before the claim: aged 16.
#ASSERT `reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2009 6 9)
-- Only child disability payment.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` `personal independence payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2005 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` `adult disability payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) (YMD 2005 1 1))
#ASSERT (`reg 15A(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))'s `the date the 3 months look back from` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT (`reg 15A(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))'s `the date the 9 months look forward from` EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
#ASSERT (`reg 15A(3): the dates for entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 7 4))'s `the date the 9 months look forward from` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 4
#ASSERT `reg 15A(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15A(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` FALSE)
-- reg 15A(5): a new claim during the 13 week period: the previous award is treated as ending the day before the new claim.
#ASSERT `reg 15A(5): the day the previous child disability payment award is treated as having ended` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 6 9
#ASSERT `reg 15A(5): the day the previous child disability payment award is treated as having ended` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
-- The day before the 1st of a month: end of the previous month.
#ASSERT `reg 15A(5): the day the previous child disability payment award is treated as having ended` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1) TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

§ `Tests of regulation 15B`

-- Scottish adult disability living allowance, ended not more than 2 years before the claim; no PIP since; born 9 April 1948.
-- C turned 65 on 9 April 2013, so was 64 on 8 April 2013.
#ASSERT `reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2023 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE (YMD 1948 4 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2023 6 9) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE (YMD 1948 4 9))
-- Born 8 April 1948: C turned 65 on 8 April 2013, so was 65 on that day.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE (YMD 1948 4 8))
-- Born 7 April 1948: 65 since 7 April 2013.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE (YMD 1948 4 7))
-- Born in 1990: 22 on 8 April 2013.
#ASSERT `reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1)
-- Entitled to personal independence payment since the award ended: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 TRUE (YMD 1990 1 1))
-- Another benefit.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `child disability payment` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) 2 FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1))
-- Under reg 26A the 2 years become 1 year (the input): exactly 1 year before is within, one day more is not.
#ASSERT `reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2024 6 10) (YMD 2025 6 10) 1 FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (YMD 2024 6 9) (YMD 2025 6 10) 1 FALSE (YMD 1990 1 1))
#ASSERT `reg 15(1)(b): the number of years` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `reg 15A(1)(b): the number of years` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `reg 15B(1)(b): the number of years` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the day 8th April 2013` EQUALS YMD 2013 4 8
#ASSERT (`reg 15B(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))'s `the date the 3 months look back from` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT (`reg 15B(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10))'s `the date the 9 months look forward from` EQUALS YMD 2025 6 10
#ASSERT (`reg 15B(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 7 4))'s `the date the 9 months look forward from` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 4
#ASSERT `reg 15B(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 15B(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 15B(6): the day the previous Scottish adult disability living allowance award is treated as having ended` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 6 9
#ASSERT `reg 15B(6): the day the previous Scottish adult disability living allowance award is treated as having ended` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 6 10) FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1

§ `Tests of which provision fixes the prescribed date`

-- (reg 15 applies, reg 15A applies, reg 15B applies, stage)
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE FALSE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` TRUE FALSE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15(2)`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` TRUE FALSE FALSE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15(3)`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE TRUE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15A(2)`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE TRUE FALSE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15A(3)`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE TRUE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15B(2)`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE FALSE TRUE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `regulation 15B(3)`
-- More than one applies: the text does not say which prevails (fork F-14).
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` TRUE TRUE FALSE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` TRUE FALSE TRUE `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` EQUALS `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`
#ASSERT `regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` FALSE TRUE TRUE `determining entitlement under the new claim` EQUALS `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`
